diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..3958154 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,21 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Delivery
+
+When a subscribed event happens, Fizzy POSTs JSON to the payload URL exactly once.
+
+Generic endpoints receive the event. Slack incoming-webhook URLs receive `{ "text": "..." }`. Campfire message URLs receive `{ "body": "..." }`. Basecamp chat line URLs receive `{ "content": "..." }`.
+
+Each request includes:
+
+- `User-Agent: fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook`
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the event time
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body, using the webhook signing secret
+
+The delivery log records the outcome. Logs are kept for one week. A webhook is switched off after ten consecutive failures within an hour, and can be turned back on with the activation endpoint.
+
 ## `GET /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks`
 
 Returns a paginated list of webhooks for a board.
